<DocsLayout
  title="<attestto-verify> Component"
  description="Full API reference for the attestto-verify Web Component. Attributes, events, CSS parts, and usage examples."
  currentPath="/docs/verify/verify-component/"
  structuredData={structuredData}
>
  <h1>&lt;attestto-verify&gt;</h1>
  <p class="docs-hero-sub">
    Client-side document verification. Drop a PDF and get hash, signatures,
    forensic audit results, and a trust level &mdash; all without leaving the browser.
  </p>

  <h2>Basic usage</h2>

  <CodeBlock lang="HTML">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-tag">&lt;attestto-verify&gt;&lt;/attestto-verify&gt;</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <p>That is a fully functional verifier. Every attribute below is optional.</p>

  <h2>Attributes</h2>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Attribute</th>
        <th>Type</th>
        <th>Default</th>
        <th>Description</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>hash</code></td>
        <td><code>string</code></td>
        <td>&mdash;</td>
        <td>Pre-computed SHA-256 hash to verify against. If provided, the component compares the file hash to this value.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>allow-plugins</code></td>
        <td><code>boolean</code></td>
        <td><code>true</code></td>
        <td>Enable or disable the plugin system. Set to <code>false</code> to use only the built-in verification pipeline.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>theme</code></td>
        <td><code>"light" | "dark"</code></td>
        <td><code>"light"</code></td>
        <td>Color scheme for the component. Can also be controlled with CSS custom properties.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>root-ca</code></td>
        <td><code>string</code></td>
        <td>&mdash;</td>
        <td>URL to a custom root CA certificate bundle (PEM). Used to validate signer certificates against your own trust store.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <CodeBlock lang="HTML" title="All attributes">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-tag">&lt;attestto-verify</span>
  <span class="c-attr">hash</span>=<span class="c-str">"e3b0c44298fc1c149afbf4c8996fb92427ae41e4649b934ca495991b7852b855"</span>
  <span class="c-attr">allow-plugins</span>=<span class="c-str">"true"</span>
  <span class="c-attr">theme</span>=<span class="c-str">"dark"</span>
  <span class="c-attr">root-ca</span>=<span class="c-str">"https://example.com/ca-bundle.pem"</span>
<span class="c-tag">&gt;&lt;/attestto-verify&gt;</span>`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <h2>What it does</h2>
  <p>When a user drops a PDF onto the component, the verification pipeline runs four stages:</p>

  <div class="docs-steps">
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">1</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Hash</strong> &mdash; Computes a SHA-256 hash of the entire file. If a <code>hash</code> attribute is set, compares the result and reports match/mismatch.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">2</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Signatures</strong> &mdash; Detects and verifies PAdES and PKCS#7 digital signatures. Extracts signer names, certificates, timestamps, and chain validity.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">3</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Forensic audit</strong> &mdash; Scans for JavaScript injection, OpenAction scripts, embedded executables, form actions pointing to external URLs, and encryption flags.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="docs-step">
      <div class="docs-step-num">4</div>
      <div class="docs-step-body">
        <p><strong>Plugins</strong> &mdash; If enabled, passes results through registered plugins (DID resolution, trust registries, blockchain anchors) to elevate the trust level.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>Events</h2>
  <p>The component dispatches Custom Events that bubble and cross Shadow DOM boundaries:</p>

  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr>
        <th>Event</th>
        <th>Detail</th>
        <th>When</th>
      </tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td><code>verification-started</code></td>
        <td><code>&#123; fileName: string, fileSize: number &#125;</code></td>
        <td>A file is dropped or selected and processing begins.</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td><code>verification-complete</code></td>
        <td><code>&#123; hash: string, signatures: Signature[], plugins: PluginResult[] &#125;</code></td>
        <td>All verification stages have finished.</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h3>Listening for events</h3>

  <CodeBlock lang="JavaScript">
<Fragment set:html={`<span class="c-kw">const</span> verifier = document.<span class="c-fn">querySelector</span>(<span class="c-str">'attestto-verify'</span>)

verifier.<span class="c-fn">addEventListener</span>(<span class="c-str">'verification-started'</span>, (e) <span class="c-op">=&gt;</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Processing:'</span>, e.detail.fileName)
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Size:'</span>, e.detail.fileSize, <span class="c-str">'bytes'</span>)
<span class="c-br">}</span>)

verifier.<span class="c-fn">addEventListener</span>(<span class="c-str">'verification-complete'</span>, (e) <span class="c-op">=&gt;</span> <span class="c-br">{</span>
  <span class="c-kw">const</span> <span class="c-br">{</span> hash, signatures, plugins <span class="c-br">}</span> = e.detail

  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'SHA-256:'</span>, hash)
  console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Signatures found:'</span>, signatures.length)

  <span class="c-cm">// Check trust level</span>
  <span class="c-kw">const</span> trusted = signatures.<span class="c-fn">some</span>(s <span class="c-op">=&gt;</span> s.trustLevel <span class="c-op">===</span> <span class="c-str">'trusted'</span>)
  <span class="c-kw">if</span> (trusted) <span class="c-br">{</span>
    console.<span class="c-fn">log</span>(<span class="c-str">'Document is trusted'</span>)
  <span class="c-br">}</span>

  <span class="c-cm">// Send hash to your backend for recording</span>
  <span class="c-fn">fetch</span>(<span class="c-str">'/api/verify'</span>, <span class="c-br">{</span>
    method: <span class="c-str">'POST'</span>,
    body: JSON.<span class="c-fn">stringify</span>(<span class="c-br">{</span> hash, signatureCount: signatures.length <span class="c-br">}</span>)
  <span class="c-br">}</span>)
<span class="c-br">}</span>)`} />
  </CodeBlock>

  <Callout type="privacy">
    <strong>Privacy note:</strong> Only the hash leaves the browser in the example above &mdash; and only because your code
    explicitly sends it. The component itself makes zero network requests.
  </Callout>

